# https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/isoAutomationLevel node1834
node1834 [ shape=none, color=black label=< <table color='#666666' cellborder='0' cellspacing='0' border='1'><tr><td colspan='2' bgcolor='grey'><B>isoAutomationLevel</B></td></tr><tr><td href='https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/isoAutomationLevel' bgcolor='#eeeeee' colspan='2'><font point-size='10' color='#6666ff'>https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/isoAutomationLevel</font></td></tr><tr><td align='left'>rdfs:comment</td><td align='left'>&quot;ISO level of automation.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:definition</td><td align='left'>&quot;ISO level of automation.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:note</td><td align='left'>&quot;The level of automation describes a spectrum of system capability, defining
the degree of control and decision-making authority a system possesses
relative to an external control.

This classification helps to define the roles and responsibilities of both the
human operator and the automated system. It is a critical component for risk
assessment, regulatory compliance, and user interface design.&quot;@en</td></tr></table> > ] 
